.TH GIMME 1 "2026-08-27" "gimme 2.4.0" "gimme Manual"
.SH NAME
gimme \- unified package manager for macOS (orchestrator)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gimme
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR] [\fIFLAGS\fR]
.sp
.B gimme
\fIMANAGER\fR \fIARGS...\fR  \(ba passthrough to a backend manager

.SH DESCRIPTION
gimme is a pure-orchestration package manager: it does not download, build,
or shelve anything itself. It drives real package managers \(em Homebrew, Go,
uv, Cargo, bun, npm, pnpm, Yarn, RubyGems, Composer, Deno, pipx, aqua, ubi,
and the Mac App Store \(em through one interface and exposes them as a single
unified namespace. A package that exists on several managers is resolved
automatically (configurable priority); an explicit
.B --from
pins the choice, and the choice is remembered per package.
.PP
Results are live-queried and cached on disk with per-type TTLs (5 min for
list/outdated results, 1 h for per-package registry version lookups, 6 h for
App Store lookups). Mutating operations invalidate the affected entries.
A GUI app (Gimme.app) wraps the same engine.
.PP
Missing backends are bootstrapped on demand: installing a package through a
manager that is not installed first offers to install that manager.

.SH COMMANDS
.SS \fBinstall\fR \fIname\fR [\fI--from\fR \fImanager\fR] [\fI--version\fR \fIv\fR]
Install a package, asking each available manager in priority order.
.B --from
forces a specific manager and records the preference.
.SS \fBuninstall\fR \fIname\fR [\fI--from\fR \fImanager\fR]
Remove a package.
.SS \fBupgrade\fR [\fIname\fR]
With a name, upgrade that package. With no name, upgrade every outdated
package across all managers (partial failures are reported per package).
.SS \fBupdate\fR [\fI--self\fR]
Alias of bare
.BR upgrade .
.B update --self
checks the latest GitHub release and replaces the gimme binary itself
(SHA256SUMS-verified download).
.SS \fBlist\fR [\fI--from\fR \fImanager\fR]
List packages installed across all managers (or one), as
\fI[manager] name version\fR lines.
.SS \fBoutdated\fR [\fI--from\fR \fImanager\fR]
Show packages with a newer version available, as
\fI[manager] name installed -> latest\fR lines. Per-package registry lookups
are cached for 1 h;
.B --force
re-asks every registry.
.SS \fBsearch\fR \fIquery\fR [\fI--all\fR]
Search the highest-priority manager that has the package; with
.BR --all ,
search every manager.
.SS \fBfind\fR \fIquery\fR
Search every capable manager at once, exact name matches ranked first
("which managers provide jq?"). Respects
.B --json
and
.BR --force .
.SS \fBinfo\fR \fIname\fR [\fI--from\fR \fImanager\fR]
Show a package's latest version and description.
.SS \fBforget\fR \fIname\fR | \fB--all\fR
Drop remembered per-package manager preferences.
.SS \fBconsolidate\fR
Report packages installed through more than one manager in the same
ecosystem, with recommended install/uninstall commands. Makes no changes.
.SS \fBdoctor\fR
Per-manager availability and version, plus detected runtime version
managers (mise/asdf) which gimme coexists with but does not manage.
.SS \fBconfig\fR [\fIset priority \fIa,b,c\fR] [\fIset ecosystem.\fIeco\fR \fImanager\fR] [\fIshow ecosystems\fR]
With no arguments, print the current config. Manager resolution priority and
per-ecosystem consolidation targets are settable.
.SS \fBhelp\fR, \fB--version\fR
Usage text; version string.

.SH PASSTHROUGH
.TP
.B gimme <manager> <args...>
Forward arguments verbatim to the underlying tool, e.g.
.B gimme brew tap
or
.BR "gimme cargo build --release" .
gimme does not parse or model passthrough commands. Managers:
homebrew, go, uv, cargo, bun, npm, pnpm, yarn, gem, composer, deno, pipx,
aqua, ubi, appstore (mas).

.SH FLAGS
.TP
.BR \-\-from " <manager>"
Restrict a command to one manager.
.TP
.BR \-\-all
search: query every manager. forget: drop all preferences.
.TP
.BR \-\-refresh
Bypass the list/outdated result cache for this run.
.TP
.BR \-\-force
Bypass every cache layer, including per-package registry lookups (implies
.BR \-\-refresh ).
.B \-\-no\-cache
is an alias.
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Machine-readable JSON output for list/outdated/search/info/install/doctor/consolidate.
.TP
.BR \-\-version " <v>"
install: pin to a version.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Non-interactive; auto-confirm bootstrap prompts.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error, or package/manager not found.
.TP
.B 2
Install failure, network error, checksum mismatch, permission error.
.TP
.B 3
Conflict.
.TP
.B 4
Lock contention.
.TP
.B 70
Unknown error.

.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/gimme/config.toml
Manager priority, disabled managers, cache TTLs, ecosystem targets.
.TP
.B ~/.config/gimme/preferences.toml
Remembered per-package manager choices (see
.BR forget ).
.TP
.B ~/.cache/gimme/
TTL disk cache. Safe to delete; it refills.

